  "bug_discussion": "Official fixing record: https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/10127\n\nWinch: Fix Wasm vector loads to operate on 64-bits (#10127)\n\n\n\nPreliminary source observation: A January 2025 Winch refactor derived 1, 2, or 4-byte access sizes for SIMD vector-extend loads that actually read 8 bytes. The PR says the correction restores bounds enforcement; its WAT disassembly tests use an out-of-bounds linear-memory address. Whether host bytes can be observed is still unproven.\nSecurity impact, input reachability, earliest effective fix, and a three-revision oracle require independent review.",
